Project README
This project uses Playwright for test automation and k6 for performance testing. Follow the instructions below to set up your environment and install the required dependencies.

Prerequisites
Node.js (LTS version recommended)
npm (Node Package Manager)
k6 for performance testing
Installation
1. Clone the Repository
Clone the project repository and navigate into the project directory:

git clone <repository_url>
cd <repository_directory>
2. Install Project Dependencies
Install the project dependencies using npm:

npm install
3. Install Playwright as a Dev Dependency
Install Playwright using npm with the --save-dev flag:

npm install --save-dev @playwright/test
After installing Playwright, install the necessary browsers:

npx playwright install
4. Set Up Environment Variables
Create a .env file in the root of your project to store environment-specific variables such as API endpoints or credentials. For example:

# .env file
BASE_URL=https://app.careerflow.ai
careerFlow_USERNAME=useremail
careerFlow_PASSWORD=pw
API_KEY=your_api_key_here
Note: Make sure to update these values as needed and add the .env file to your .gitignore to prevent it from being committed.

5. Install k6 for Performance Testing
Option A: Windows (Using Chocolatey)
If you have Chocolatey installed, open an elevated Command Prompt or PowerShell and run:

choco install k6
Option B: macOS (Using Homebrew)
If you’re on macOS, install k6 via Homebrew:

brew install k6
Option C: Manual Installation
Alternatively, download the Windows binary from the k6 installation page and add it to your system PATH.

Running the Tests
Running Playwright Tests
Execute the Playwright test suite using the following command:

npx playwright test
Running Performance Tests with k6
Navigate to the directory containing your performance_test.js script and run:

k6 run performance_test.js
Additional Information
Documentation:

Playwright Documentation
k6 Documentation
Troubleshooting:

Playwright Browsers Not Installed:
Run npx playwright install again to ensure all browsers are set up.
Environment Variables Not Loading:
Verify that the .env file exists in the project root and that you are using a package like dotenv to load variables in your Node.js scripts.
Security Note:
Ensure your .env file is added to .gitignore to prevent sensitive information from being committed to version control.

